{
  "$id": "pj.schema.v2",
  "title": "CAT OS Para Jumbles content item, schema v2",
  "description": "Schema v2 = v1 plus the pattern layer of the content engine (content/taxonomy/varc-taxonomy.json): meta.reasoning_patterns names the discourse and reasoning patterns the item exercises, meta.genre widens to the thirty taxonomy genres, and meta.quality records the adversarial review and blind solve. v1 files remain valid under v1; versions are appended, never edited. Original v1 description: One parajumble: a coherent paragraph written first, then scrambled (PARA_JUMBLES_BIBLE §10). Modern CAT default: four sentences, TITA response, no fixed opener or closer, no negative marking — carried as CONFIGURATION in meta.format, never hard-coded (Bible Recommendation 1). The metadata implements Bible §12: the twelve-dimension difficulty vector (§6), discourse macro pattern (§3), cohesion signals present (§4), engineered traps (§5), Reading-DNA traits exercised (§8), num_plausible_orderings (the master difficulty variable), and the heuristic_adversarial flag (§10: a pure surface-heuristic solve must FAIL on medium+ items). The explanation implements the four layers of Bible §11: macro pattern first, the author's movement sentence by sentence, the most tempting wrong orders walked to their breaking point, and the trap named as a reusable defense. links documents one identifiable device per consecutive pair (CAT_VARC_BIBLE §22) WITH its reliability, because every signal is a local heuristic that can be weaponized (Bible §4). Device enum extends CONTENT_DATABASE_SCHEMA §10.2's six with given_new_flow, demonstrative_reference, lexical_bridge and parallel_structure, per Bible §4 — additive, on a new schema file. Validation subset: see src/core/content-loader/validator.js.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "meta",
    "sentences",
    "correct_order",
    "links",
    "explanation",
    "mentor"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "const": 2
    },
    "meta": {
      "type": "object",
